  "schema_version": 1,
  "_doc": "Province buildings (design/gdd/provinces.md rules 7-10, States; design/quick-specs/province-building-catalogue.md; provinces-runtime Stage 2), read by ProvinceBuildings. kinds: group (production, logistics, society, cultivation), track (prices the level: Sects F2 free_level, x track_surcharge per level above; no highest level), kind (permanent keeps its gain while unpaid; upkept counts 0 while unpaid), work (the Travel & Map work its effect is written as at the places it acts on, MapWorks reads it), acts (seat: the province's seat settlement; sites: the province's sites of the listed place kinds; all_sites; province: the province itself), cost_lt, growth, materials, rarity_min, seasons (permanent: seasons x level; upkept: 1 + floor(level / 3)), upkeep (linh thach a level a season) or upkeep_site_frac (of the acting sites' base value a level), staff (population units a level, F4), live (false: placed for slots but not billed, not ordered and with no effect until its stage makes it live), out (F4 out[b]: base value a level of the listed good kind, counted in the province's production only). ruin_seasons: unpaid seasons that ruin an upkept building. start_enabled: place rule 10's starting buildings at world generation. All numbers are guesses (Provinces OQ 1). start_level (user request 2026-11-24: starting levels follow the lore): a starting building's level is max(1, round(the payer sect's authored level in the kind's track x per_track_level)), x away_factor outside the sect's seat province; unheld land stays at 1. lore_specialty and lore_craft: the halls (and lore buildings) a sect starts with at its seat province, from its authored specialty and the craft text of world_history.json (keyword, kind; the first keywords of the list that match each add their kind once); a landing is placed only on a coast or river. sect_extra: authored lore extras by sect key (held_provinces: kinds placed in every province the sect holds). These are a proposal for the user's review. start_level.flat_groups: groups that start at level 1 whatever the sect (production, 2026-11-24 under the user's delegation: lore levels on mines and fields with site growth tripled stone minting and doubled the world's money in the sim; they grow in play instead). Stage 4 (2026-11-24, under the user's delegation): the sect halls are live. value_per_member: a hall level's season value per member of the sect whose seat it stands at (how sects rank it against other buildings). seat_stats: sheet rows per level for members at their sect's seat (crafting there); member_stats: per level for every member; market_kind: the crafted kind whose success rate ps rises in the markets of its region, ps' = 1 - (1 - ps) / (1 + market_ps_k x levels); tier_per_level: new members' technique tier roll; step_per_level: members' breakthrough step at the bottleneck; intake_per_level: the sect's intake weight. repair_frac: a ruined building's repair costs this share of its level's price and its build seasons. All guesses. cap_b (Stage 5): population capacity a level (F3).",
